    <section class="section system-section" id="system" aria-label="Session continuity illustration">
      <div class="split-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / THE COMPANY BRAIN</span><h2 id="system-title">The project remembers.<br>The agent continues.</h2></div><p>Sessions end. The knowledge behind the work should stay with the project, ready for the next person or agent.</p></div>
      <div class="system-flow" role="group" aria-label="A session records project knowledge and a later session recovers context"><div class="session-node"><span class="eyebrow">SESSION A</span><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><strong>Investigate<br>&amp; record</strong><small>Temporary session memory</small></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="project-node"><span class="eyebrow">SHARED PROJECT STATE</span><div class="state-symbol" aria-hidden="true">◎</div><strong>Continuing knowledge</strong><div class="state-tags"><span>Work</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Decisions</span></div></div><span class="flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="session-node"><span class="eyebrow">SESSION B</span><span class="node-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌘</span><strong>Recover<br>&amp; continue</strong><small>Fresh context for the task</small></div></div>
      <p class="section-footnote">Context views select what a task needs. Permissions and freshness still apply.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section craft-section" id="paper-craft" aria-labelledby="paper-craft-title">
      <div class="split-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / SOFTWARE WORK</span><h2 id="paper-craft-title">Meet Craft.<br>Make the model explicit.</h2></div><p>Craft describes the concepts, rules and behavior an implementation must preserve. The Lab keeps the context around that work.</p></div>
      <div class="craft-grid"><article><div class="code-heading"><span>01 / CALCULATION</span><span aria-hidden="true">ƒ(x)</span></div><h3>Evaluate a request.</h3><p>A capacity check answers whether a request fits. It calculates a result without changing the state.</p><div class="code-line"><span>capacity.check</span><span>→ result</span></div></article><article><div class="code-heading"><span>02 / OPERATION</span><span aria-hidden="true">↦</span></div><h3>Change the state.</h3><p>Reserving that capacity performs a change. Its effects and constraints belong in the model.</p><div class="code-line"><span>capacity.reserve</span><span>→ effect</span></div></article></div>
      <div class="section-tail"><p>A conceptual example. Product and release work continues.</p><a class="inline-link" href="../craft-documentation-proposal/craft-model.html#definition">Read the Craft model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </section>

