<section id="lab" class="page-width research-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="lab-title">
<p class="section-marker">01 / The company brain</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="lab-title">Keep the knowledge<br>behind the work.</h2>
<div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">A task list leaves some important questions open. What do the goals mean? Why was a decision taken, and what evidence supports the account of what happened? The project needs those answers too.</p><p>The Lab gives that knowledge a continuing structure. Definitions state the important meanings. Connected records let the next reader inspect attempts, claim support and decisions governing change.</p><p>When the work changes hands, those connections give the next participant a place to begin.</p></div>
<div class="home-model-map"><figure class="company-brain-map" aria-labelledby="company-brain-map-title">
<div class="brain-map-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Inside the company brain</p><h3 id="company-brain-map-title">One connected body of knowledge.</h3></div>
<div class="brain-map-field">
<svg class="brain-map-connections" viewBox="0 0 600 520" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
<path data-brain-branch="people" d="M155 134C174 150 211 165 240 176"/>
<path data-brain-branch="agents" d="M445 134C426 150 389 165 360 176"/>
<path data-brain-branch="knowledge" d="M248 238C211 282 150 303 90 324"/>
<path data-brain-branch="work" d="M300 314V410"/>
<path data-brain-branch="decisions" d="M352 238C389 282 450 303 510 324"/>
</svg>
<button class="brain-map-node brain-people" data-brain-part="people" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="brain-map-detail" disabled><span class="brain-node-icon"><img src="assets/role-icons/people.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="192" height="192" decoding="async"></span><strong>People</strong><small>Intentions &amp; review</small></button>
<button class="brain-map-node brain-agents" data-brain-part="agents" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="brain-map-detail" disabled><span class="brain-node-icon"><img src="assets/role-icons/agents.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="192" height="192" decoding="async"></span><strong>Agents</strong><small>Scoped sessions</small></button>
<a class="brain-map-core" href="#lab"><img class="brain-core-art" src="assets/role-icons/core.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="192" height="192" decoding="async"><span class="brain-core-caption"><strong>Shared project state</strong><small>Durable knowledge</small></span></a>
<button class="brain-map-node brain-knowledge" data-brain-part="knowledge" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="brain-map-detail" disabled><span class="brain-node-icon"><img src="assets/role-icons/knowledge.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="192" height="192" decoding="async"></span><strong>Knowledge</strong><small>Meaning &amp; evidence</small></button>
<button class="brain-map-node brain-work" data-brain-part="work" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="brain-map-detail" disabled><span class="brain-node-icon"><img src="assets/role-icons/work.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="192" height="192" decoding="async"></span><strong>Work</strong><small>Plans &amp; attempts</small></button>
<button class="brain-map-node brain-decisions" data-brain-part="decisions" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="brain-map-detail" disabled><span class="brain-node-icon"><img src="assets/role-icons/decisions.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="192" height="192" decoding="async"></span><strong>Decisions</strong><small>Review &amp; change</small></button>
</div>
<p class="brain-map-hint">Choose a part to explore its responsibility. Select it again when you want the full picture.</p>
<div id="brain-map-detail" class="brain-map-detail" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><h3>Knowledge, work and decisions stay connected.</h3><p>People express intentions and review results. Agents work within permission. The project retains the meanings, evidence and decisions needed to continue.</p></div>
<figcaption>A map of roles around shared project state. <a href="governance-lab-reference.html#system-map">Explore the full system map <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<figure class="brain-knowledge-cycle" aria-labelledby="knowledge-cycle-title"><h3 id="knowledge-cycle-title">How the connections become useful</h3><div class="knowledge-cycle-flow"><div class="knowledge-cycle-part cycle-knowledge"><span class="cycle-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 5C8 2 4 3 2 4v16c3-2 7-2 10 0 3-2 7-2 10 0V4c-2-1-6-2-10 1Zm0 0v15M5 8h4M5 12h4m6-4h4m-4 4h4"/></svg></span><strong>Knowledge</strong><p>Definitions, sources<br>and lessons</p></div><span class="knowledge-cycle-link">informs <b aria-hidden="true">→</b></span><div class="knowledge-cycle-part cycle-work"><span class="cycle-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m14 4 6 6-3 3-6-6Zm-3 3-7 7 3 3 7-7M3 21l4-4"/></svg></span><strong>Work</strong><p>Plans, attempts<br>and evidence</p></div><span class="knowledge-cycle-link">supports review <b aria-hidden="true">→</b></span><div class="knowledge-cycle-part cycle-decisions"><span class="cycle-icon"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 5H4v17h16V5h-4"/><rect x="8" y="2" width="8" height="5" rx="2"/><path d="m8 14 3 3 6-7"/></svg></span><strong>Decisions</strong><p>Review, acceptance<br>and next steps</p></div></div><div class="knowledge-cycle-return"><span aria-hidden="true">↶</span> Accepted decisions govern changes to shared project state.</div><figcaption>Each attempt leaves evidence to examine. An accepted change follows its own authority route.</figcaption></figure>
</div></section>

<section id="how" class="lab-section" aria-labelledby="how-title"><div class="page-width section-grid">
<p class="section-marker">02 / How it works</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="how-title">From an intention<br>to an accountable next step.</h2>
<ol class="product-steps"><li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>State what the work means.</h3><p>Start with the intention and the meaning of success. If the task says “complete,” give people a criterion they can examine.</p><a class="text-link" href="governance-lab-reference.html#governance">Definitions and authority <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li><li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Connect the work to its evidence.</h3><p>Follow an assessment back to its sources, methods and observations. The finding should stay connected to its actual support.</p><a class="text-link" href="governance-lab-reference.html#evidence">Provenance and evidence <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li><li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Make change explicit.</h3><p>Proposing a change, accepting it and deploying it have different consequences. Each needs its declared rules and authority.</p><a class="text-link" href="governance-lab-reference.html#change">Lifecycle and change <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li><li><span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span><div><h3>Continue from usable context.</h3><p>The next session needs relevant project knowledge, usable context and current permission. Check those before continuing.</p><a class="text-link" href="governance-lab-reference.html#agent">Agent work and context <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li></ol>
</div></div></section>

<section id="continuity" class="page-width research-section section-grid" aria-labelledby="continuity-title">
<p class="section-marker">03 / Working with agents</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="continuity-title">The project remembers.<br>The agent continues.</h2><div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">An agent session ends. The knowledge needed to continue belongs in the project.</p><p>Project State keeps that knowledge. Context Views select information for a task, and Ontology Views show relevant concepts and declared connections. A fresh session recovers context through those views.</p><p>Working memory belongs to the session. Expired views or changed permissions require refresh or a pause. A saved lesson also needs examination: later work should record its use and assess its benefit.</p></div>
<figure class="session-handoff"><div><small>Session A</small><strong>Investigate &amp; record</strong><span>Temporary session memory</span></div><div class="handoff-state"><small>Project state</small><strong>Continuing knowledge</strong><span>Work, evidence &amp; decisions</span></div><div><small>Session B</small><strong>Recover &amp; continue</strong><span>Fresh views &amp; applicable permission</span></div><figcaption>A handoff between sessions. The recorded project knowledge provides continuity.</figcaption></figure>
</div></section>

<section id="craft" class="lab-section" aria-labelledby="craft-title"><div class="page-width section-grid">
<p class="section-marker">04 / Software work</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="craft-title">Meet Craft</h2><div class="reading-copy"><p class="section-lead">Craft is the software-design product within the Lab. Its explicit models describe the concepts, rules and behavior an implementation must preserve.</p><p>The Lab keeps the project context, evidence and decisions around that work. A model’s capacity check, for example, evaluates a request through a Calculation. Reserving the capacity changes state through an Operation. Those separate responsibilities give the implementation a clear reference.</p></div><a class="ds-button" href="../craft-documentation-proposal/craft-model.html">Read the Craft model <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
</div></section>

<section id="explore" class="page-width research-section section-grid explore-section" aria-labelledby="explore-title">
<p class="section-marker">05 / Explore the Lab</p>
<div class="section-content"><h2 id="explore-title">See the system<br>from the inside.</h2><div class="work-links"><a href="start-here.html"><span><small>Begin here</small><strong>Get to know CyberAlchemy Lab</strong><span>A short introduction to the complete model.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="incident-walkthrough.html"><span><small>A concrete example</small><strong>Follow an incident</strong><span>See definitions, evidence, permissions and changes fit together.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="governance-lab-reference.html#system-map"><span><small>A visual explanation</small><strong>Explore the system map</strong><span>Inspect the model through different lenses.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="company-brain.html"><span><small>The product story</small><strong>Why we are building a company brain</strong><span>The problem, the approach and its connection to alignment.</span></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div>
<p class="product-origin">CyberAlchemy is a research lab studying intelligence and how people and machines work together. <a href="research.html">Our research, culture and ambition →</a></p>
</div></section>
